WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.670
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.150
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.850
between Burger King in the US and the UK.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.475
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.720
In the UK, we have three drink sizes.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.100
We have a small,

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.341
which is 250 milliliters.

00:00:21.341 --> 00:00:22.899
Joe Avella: This is a US small.

00:00:22.899 --> 00:00:25.660
Harry: We have a regular,
which is 400 milliliters.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.420
Joe: This is a US medium.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.812
Harry: And we have a large.

00:00:29.812 --> 00:00:32.053
Joe: And here [groans]

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.836
is a US large.

00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:36.561
Burger King.

00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:38.780
Harry: Now, in the UK, we
have three sizes of fries,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.240
small, regular, and large.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.913
Joe: Here's a Burger King small fry.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.683
Here's a Burger King medium fry.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.543
And a Burger King large fry.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.200
Harry: So, of the three sizes
of fries that we were given,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.050
I'm actually not sure
which one is the regular

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.467
and which one is the small,

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:01.880
because these two kinda look identical.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.122
We're going to weigh them all.

00:01:04.122 --> 00:01:05.440
We're gonna start with this

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.049
orange-bottomed bag.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.494
80...

00:01:14.363 --> 00:01:15.500
88 grams.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.940
Now we're gonna weigh the
slightly darker orange bag

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.590
and see which size this is.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.190
So, there's only a 5-gram difference,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.897
but this one is the small.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.493
So, a large fries in the UK

00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:37.435
looks like it's around 180 grams,

00:01:37.435 --> 00:01:40.011
which is double the regular.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:41.386
[beep] I broke the scale.

00:01:41.386 --> 00:01:42.219
[laughs]

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.126
We're actually having some concerns about

00:01:52.126 --> 00:01:54.301
the sizes of the fries in the UK,

00:01:54.301 --> 00:01:56.100
because our measurements showed

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.575
that the lighter orange bag

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:59.125
actually contains more fries

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:00.440
than the darker orange bag.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.710
However, when lined up very
scientifically like this,

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.315
what we'll actually see is that

00:02:06.315 --> 00:02:09.210
the bag sizes go up in
that color order instead.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.269
So I think what's happened here is that

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:14.160
our small was actually
bigger than our regular.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.450
Joe: Wow, a lot of fry
drama over there in the UK.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.470
As you can see from our
sizes, it's pretty obvious

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.000
what the small, medium, and large is,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.870
but, of course, we're
still gonna weigh them.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.153
So let's start with the small fry.

00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:26.920
Yep.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:27.753
Boom.

00:02:27.753 --> 00:02:28.644
Rogue fry.

00:02:28.644 --> 00:02:30.094
And now the medium fry.

00:02:34.121 --> 00:02:35.340
You're making a face.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.890
I don't like that face.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.073
It's like...

00:02:39.073 --> 00:02:40.431
yeah, it's pretty similar.

00:02:40.431 --> 00:02:43.690
I know how we will solve this, but not...

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.200
not that way.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.620
Over here. Burger King
is in the hot seat, baby!

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.890
Burger King's in the hot seat!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:51.893
Large fries.

00:02:53.728 --> 00:02:56.550
So, I'm gonna do something
really tedious and boring.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.124
Two, three, four,

00:02:59.124 --> 00:03:01.390
12, 13,

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.399
20, 21, 22....

00:03:03.399 --> 00:03:04.549
35 regulars,

00:03:04.549 --> 00:03:06.250
10 kind of broken-up ones.

00:03:07.271 --> 00:03:09.570
One, two....

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.396
34 and 18, but then a lot of smaller ones.

00:03:13.396 --> 00:03:15.415
Producer: Arguably more than the medium.

00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:17.515
Joe: Whoa!

00:03:17.515 --> 00:03:18.956
That's pretty cold, Burger King.

00:03:18.956 --> 00:03:20.260
That is pretty cold.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.770
Don't act like you're surprised by this.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.380
And I know what they're gonna
say. They're gonna be like,

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.187
"Well, everyone who scoops is different."

00:03:25.187 --> 00:03:27.435
OK, but our scooper here

00:03:27.435 --> 00:03:29.076
and their scooper in the UK

00:03:29.076 --> 00:03:30.950
made a similar error.

00:03:31.825 --> 00:03:33.070
Hmm.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.000
Suspicious, right?

00:03:36.724 --> 00:03:38.705
Frygate 2020!

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.007
Harry: So, this is a Whopper in the UK.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.140
No, it's not, that's a Halloumi King.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.482
Is this the Whopper?

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.570
Have they forgotten the f---ing Whoppers?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:55.683
Burger King!

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.380
So, what we're going to
do is weigh a Whopper

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.998
and see how much a
Whopper weighs in the UK.

00:04:02.998 --> 00:04:05.581
[burger thuds]

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:09.530
Joe: All right, let's take
a look at the US Whopper.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.631
First thing I'm gonna
do, I'm gonna weigh it.

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:15.140
Oh, yeah.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.250
That's a Whopper.

00:04:17.558 --> 00:04:18.391
Booyah.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.460
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait,

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:22.330
gotta be scientific about it.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.865
Harry: In the UK, you
can get Burger King's

00:04:23.865 --> 00:04:25.573
chicken fries in three sizes.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.500
A six-piece box,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.710
a nine-piece box,

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.085
or if you're really hungry,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.243
a 20-piece box.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.850
Joe: In the US, according
to the Burger King website,

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.600
they have three sizes of chicken fries.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.025
We went to, like, five Burger Kings.

00:04:44.025 --> 00:04:44.858
Two.

00:04:44.858 --> 00:04:47.580
And both of them said that
they only have one size,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.420
the nine-piece chicken fries.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.620
I don't know why that is.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.086
And after

00:04:53.086 --> 00:04:55.771
Burger King Frygate 2020,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.892
I'm gonna count these.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.108
There's nine.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.740
Harry: So, what about calories?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.785
Well, for example, a large Whopper meal,

00:05:08.785 --> 00:05:11.940
the Whopper itself is 627 calories,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.356
a 180-gram serving of large fries

00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:16.731
would be 437 calories,

00:05:16.731 --> 00:05:20.636
and a large Coke would be 209 calories.

00:05:20.636 --> 00:05:22.953
That brings the total of a
large Whopper meal in the UK

00:05:22.953 --> 00:05:25.733
to 1,273 calories.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.238
Joe: And in the US Burger King,

00:05:28.238 --> 00:05:30.280
the Whopper meal comes in at a hefty

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.630
1,600 calories.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.488
That is an increase of about 378 calories,

00:05:36.488 --> 00:05:37.954
or roughly 30%.

00:05:37.954 --> 00:05:40.250
However, there are ways to
bring the calorie count down.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.300
For example, if you get
the Whopper without mayo,

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.300
you save yourself about 157 calories,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.471
taking the Whopper down to, like, 503.

00:05:47.471 --> 00:05:49.330
The drink is a major culprit.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.510
If you get a sugar-free
soda like a Diet Coke,

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.360
you immediately save
yourself 510 calories.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.820
So with these minor adjustments,

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:00.630
you can get a large Whopper
meal for about 933 calories.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.880
Harry: Now, for whatever reason,

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.768
the mayo in the UK only
comes to 6 calories.

00:06:04.768 --> 00:06:07.697
So I'm not sure what you guys
are putting in your mayo.

00:06:07.697 --> 00:06:10.219
Now, in the UK, a bacon
double cheeseburger

00:06:10.219 --> 00:06:13.343
comes in at 430 calories.

00:06:13.343 --> 00:06:15.310
Joe: And our bacon double
cheeseburger in the US

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.760
only has 404 calories.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.969
Now, this has to be a "Food Wars" first,

00:06:19.969 --> 00:06:21.905
where something in the
US has less calories

00:06:21.905 --> 00:06:23.400
than something in the UK.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.625
I do wanna point out,

00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:26.966
our bacon double cheeseburger
does not come with mayo,

00:06:26.966 --> 00:06:29.179
so I think that might
be the calorie culprit.

00:06:29.179 --> 00:06:31.040
Harry: So we finally found
something that's less calorific

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.760
in the US than the UK.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.668
Congrats, guys.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.420
Joe: Error 404, mayo not found.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.970
That's funny. Like, just
put that on the screen there

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:40.920
like an error code.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.820
Harry: Here are some things
that you can only get

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.240
at a UK Burger King.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.520
So, here we have the veggie bean burger,

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.800
which, you get these
two fried bean patties

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.015
with some lettuce, some
mayo, and some cheese.

00:06:54.015 --> 00:06:55.723
Here we have the Halloumi King,

00:06:55.723 --> 00:06:58.081
which is kind of exciting.

00:06:58.081 --> 00:07:01.860
It comes with lettuce,
mayo, onions, tomato,

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.980
and then these two fried
pieces of halloumi.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.490
They also offer that with bacon,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.870
which seems slightly counterproductive

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.153
if you're a vegetarian,

00:07:09.153 --> 00:07:10.978
but pretty delicious if you're not.

00:07:12.621 --> 00:07:13.912
Joe: Hey, Siri?

00:07:14.779 --> 00:07:16.095
[Siri beeps]

00:07:16.095 --> 00:07:18.045
What is halloumi?

00:07:19.769 --> 00:07:22.008
Siri: "Halloumi or haloumi is a semi-hard,

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.160
unripened, brined cheese
made from a mixture

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.860
of goat's and sheep's milk,

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.293
and sometimes also cow's milk."

00:07:28.293 --> 00:07:30.144
Do you want me to keep reading? [beeps]

00:07:30.144 --> 00:07:31.525
Joe: Yes.

00:07:31.525 --> 00:07:33.260
Siri: [beeps] "It has a high melting point

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.583
and so can easily be fried or grilled.

00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:38.556
This property makes it a
popular meat substitute.

00:07:38.556 --> 00:07:41.300
Rennet is used to curdle the
milk in halloumi production,

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.084
although no acid-producing bacteria

00:07:43.084 --> 00:07:45.565
are used in its preparation."

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.560
Joe: Huh, thanks.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.957
I don't want that.

00:07:51.957 --> 00:07:53.223
Harry: In the back here, we have a

00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:54.900
Chicken Royale with bacon,

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.360
which is a longer chicken
patty that's fried.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:01.110
Comes with lettuce, bacon,
and cheese and mayo.

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:04.370
To round out the burgers,
we have the Bacon King,

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.310
which is kind of like a larger version

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:07.740
of the bacon double cheeseburger,

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.070
but it also has mayo on it.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.120
And then finally
available to us right now,

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.491
we have the jalapeño chicken fries,

00:08:13.491 --> 00:08:15.730
which are kinda like their
standard chicken fries,

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.941
but with a spicy jalapeño coating.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.210
Joe: I'm furious we don't have those.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.043
That is ridiculous.

00:08:23.043 --> 00:08:25.570
How did they have the jalapeño
chicken fries and we don't?

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.100
That is ridiculous.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.830
Harry: So, on top of what
I've got in front of me,

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.130
there are also a lot of exclusives

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.000
that we have in the UK,
which I'll read for you now.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.300
The steakhouse Angus, classic cheese melt,

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:39.340
a barbecue double melt,
a chili cheese melt,

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:41.660
the Roadhouse Crispy Chicken sandwich,

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.900
the Crispy Bacon King, a Rebel Whopper,

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.560
mac 'n' cheese bites, chili cheese bites,

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.130
apple slices, a Breakfast King,

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.500
a range of breakfast sandwiches

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.060
including a bacon butty
and a sausage butty,

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.287
porridge, and an Oreo Fusion,

00:08:56.287 --> 00:08:58.711
which is like an ice cream
with some Oreos in it.

00:08:58.711 --> 00:08:59.930
It has to be said that Burger King

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.350
isn't the friendliest
place for vegetarians.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.090
They have some kind of vegetarian options,

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:07.490
like the Halloumi King
or the Rebel Whopper,

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.960
but unfortunately these
are actually cooked

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.140
in the same oil and on the
same grills as the meat.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:13.923
So it's not 100% vegetarian.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.732
Joe: Here is everything that is exclusive

00:09:16.732 --> 00:09:19.327
to the Burger King in the United States.

00:09:19.327 --> 00:09:22.219
I'm just gonna start here.

00:09:22.219 --> 00:09:23.652
Impossible Whopper.

00:09:23.652 --> 00:09:25.410
Even when we're trying to be healthy,

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.880
we still managed to figure
out a way to be unhealthy.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.230
There's stuff in our Impossible meat

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.928
that has not been approved in the UK yet.

00:09:34.991 --> 00:09:37.220
Crispy taco, here in Burger King USA only.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.709
I don't know why there's
tacos at Burger King.

00:09:40.709 --> 00:09:43.310
I don't know who's getting
a taco at Burger King.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.273
That's ridiculous.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.033
Crispy.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:48.648
The Stacker.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.010
Ooh, bacon.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:54.040
The Double Stacker.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.800
These things are so heavy.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.040
This is so much.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.515
Now, from my understanding,

00:09:58.515 --> 00:10:00.698
what separates the Stacker

00:10:00.698 --> 00:10:02.310
from the bacon double cheeseburger

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.550
is these are quarter-pound patties,

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:08.410
and also there's some sort
of Stacker sauce on here.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.006
Special Stacker sauce.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:14.543
Spicy crispy chicken sandwich.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.300
The barbecue bacon
crispy chicken sandwich.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:23.858
Spicy chicken sandwich junior.

00:10:23.858 --> 00:10:25.370
For the little guys!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.570
You can also get

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.970
an order of mozzarella sticks,

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:31.008
four, with marinara in there.

00:10:32.343 --> 00:10:33.508
Applesauce.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:35.850
Oh, yeah, breakfast.

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:36.833
Oh, good Lord.

00:10:36.833 --> 00:10:40.090
All right. So, you get
pancakes and of course syrup.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.980
And of course we're gonna do a syrup pour.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.807
Wouldn't be a "Food Wars" episode

00:10:44.807 --> 00:10:47.510
without me pouring
something on something else.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.401
Oh, OK.

00:10:49.576 --> 00:10:51.167
Ah!

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:52.170
[spits]

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.631
Ooh, yo!

00:10:55.631 --> 00:10:58.244
You like that? You like
that how that looks?

00:10:58.244 --> 00:10:59.650
Damn.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:02.600
Ah, yes, the Croissan'wich.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.540
So, as you can see,
what a Croissan'wich is,

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:09.110
is a breakfast sandwich where
a croissant is the buns.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.470
How's it look?

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.750
Look good?

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:15.208
And also, similar to McDonald's,

00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:16.141
breakfast sandwiches.

00:11:16.141 --> 00:11:19.280
They also have breakfast biscuits,

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.843
also sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:11:23.904 --> 00:11:25.279
And then last,

00:11:25.279 --> 00:11:28.495
the US Burger King breakfast burrito.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.295
Let's open it up. Let's
take a look inside!

00:11:34.306 --> 00:11:37.300
What do they got there?
They got a egg, got sausage.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.700
Oh, they got potato in here!

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:41.263
OK.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.890
I wouldn't, I would not get
this, but good for them.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.000
Good effort.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.883
Last but not least,

00:11:48.883 --> 00:11:50.220
you can also get yourself

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.610
a Hershey's sundae chocolate pie.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.260
